ng_hci: handle the LE meta events releng/15.1 leaves as stubs

LE Connection Update Complete (0x03) was a /*TBD*/ stub and LE Read
Remote Features Complete (0x04) fell through to the default. LE Remote
Connection Parameter Request (0x06) was not handled at all, and a
request nobody answers ends in a link-layer response timeout that drops
the connection.

Hand all three to NextBSD's ng_hci_le.c (this directory's src/):
0x03 logs the new parameters or the failure; 0x04 records the peer's LE
features in the neighbor cache under its LE address type, as
Read_Remote_Supported_Features does for BR/EDR; 0x06 replies with
LE_Remote_Connection_Parameter_Request_Reply carrying the peripheral's
own values when they are within the Core spec's limits, or with the
negative reply and Unacceptable Connection Parameters (0x3b) when not.

LE Long Term Key Request (0x05) stays with bluetoothd, which holds the
keys and answers on the raw hook (nextbsd/nextbsd-userland#205).

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#234). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_evnt.c, after
0001-ng_hci_evnt-LE-Enhanced-Connection-Complete.patch

